-- A line written in the form of a mixfix rule, with a literal for an input,
-- was read as a one-clause group defining a rule named Red. It checked, and
-- `Red `costs` 0` went on giving 0, where the drafter meant 1. It is refused,
-- once, at the line.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` n MEANS n
Red `costs` 0 MEANS 1

#EVAL Red `costs` 0
#EVAL Green `costs` 5
